.TH GETPID 2
.SH NAME
getpid \- get process identification
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "getpid( )"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B getpid
returns the process ID of the current process.
Most often it is
used to generate uniquely-named temporary files.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
mktemp(3)
.SH ASSEMBLER
(getpid = 20.)
.TP
PDP-11:
.nf
sys getpid
R0 = process ID
.fi
.TP
8086:
.nf
BX = 20
int 0Xf1
AX = process ID
.fi
.sp
